[{:db/id "q-8257/selection/b966f07f99f5777daa432cd875ce149e29d5d2d68740c817a8560493287ac468" :answer/id #uuid "629fbaf2-2c6d-55d1-9b71-70c01a308e3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.98" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8257/selection/a391946085ae0fb69488ecbf1c10a03470c3f68ac29b297598d73e115174e8c6" :answer/id #uuid "8a21fbbb-d371-51b9-be2d-3daefcb68885" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8257/selection/0ab5179a643a123ebc5759e29002b95a10fa75402ca63a1ff627d27904361aec" :answer/id #uuid "4439b33b-d0dc-584e-bf17-75abccae95ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8257/selection/a396d0598089dcf7fd80ac428e69110b5ef13338c3a7bb03e2ab510410ef3602" :answer/id #uuid "e55d2641-8c5e-5ecd-8563-264a2982b09c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8257/selection/a0b3dca4af88dbe5fcf628fbef35927de86ad005a83e7b7734ad21aa107addf0" :answer/id #uuid "21b98ea1-a4d8-56dc-81d4-2476c276adf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.63" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8257/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "23a6f6e5-5519-5213-b609-1da104a9ecf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8257/selection/a396d0598089dcf7fd80ac428e69110b5ef13338c3a7bb03e2ab510410ef3602" :answer-field/choices ["q-8257/selection/b966f07f99f5777daa432cd875ce149e29d5d2d68740c817a8560493287ac468" "q-8257/selection/a391946085ae0fb69488ecbf1c10a03470c3f68ac29b297598d73e115174e8c6" "q-8257/selection/0ab5179a643a123ebc5759e29002b95a10fa75402ca63a1ff627d27904361aec" "q-8257/selection/a396d0598089dcf7fd80ac428e69110b5ef13338c3a7bb03e2ab510410ef3602" "q-8257/selection/a0b3dca4af88dbe5fcf628fbef35927de86ad005a83e7b7734ad21aa107addf0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8257" :question/id #uuid "182ca814-357c-5897-88e6-eaddeb481aa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-8257" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find, in radians to two decimal places, the argument of $z=-3+4\\text{i}.$ \n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/assets/373ea8254a9816f67bfbcaf993348f409c1047284d09c43e5d41e68b15c5af58.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane. Therefore $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<\\pi .$ If $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan⁡(\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & ≈0.927\\,30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)≈\\pi -0.927\\,30≈2.21\n$$\n\nto two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8257/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "833ac63c-235b-5059-ab7c-56eb1e44d79e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8257"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8454"] :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/assets/d096d76118bc06b2d5c79d5017c0178d96fc84bff6f97d563b7b872d26e75d20.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane. Therefore $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<2\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the positive real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan⁡(\\frac{5}{7})≈0.620\\,25.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=2\\pi -0.620\\,25≈5.66\n$$\n\nto two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-319517/field-1/5627864fcdd0a711b4e460490fbdcf4b647b6c518f92f82f09bc3957623966bb" :answer/id #uuid "0d47d315-fd39-5905-91d6-6c076260040d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319517/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8cbf8899-710c-5264-b7a5-b0a51ef658f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319517/field-1/5627864fcdd0a711b4e460490fbdcf4b647b6c518f92f82f09bc3957623966bb" :answer-field/choices ["q-319517/field-1/5627864fcdd0a711b4e460490fbdcf4b647b6c518f92f82f09bc3957623966bb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319517" :question/id #uuid "847a1127-b379-55f0-bcc6-f21c519a7a9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-319517" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=-8-5\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/assets/c598c3b872cd2c4b3af08d8b2dbaf6a79512fe382473320feb526f31e5ece246.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the third quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\pi <arg⁡(z)<\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan\\,(\\frac{5}{8})=0.558\\,599…\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=\\pi +0.558\\,599…≈3.70,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-319517/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a560db4d-e9d3-5d89-b2cd-c886f32db9df"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319517"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319519/field-1/81758f67bd42269c828704bfccbe9dd868769d094ce91f8cf86cac7da22bac29" :answer/id #uuid "de0ed0cf-1d97-569c-a057-ee624747eaab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319519/field-1/867645cc65f2523d2da0f0bf9f79dcff4e4758e45f7d0d53126cc6ed4f8a9875" :answer/id #uuid "c8ebed28-0492-5f2d-9c60-07b9616962f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319519/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "16b8fa78-aa93-597b-835f-b55c9802a212" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319519/field-1/81758f67bd42269c828704bfccbe9dd868769d094ce91f8cf86cac7da22bac29" :answer-field/choices ["q-319519/field-1/81758f67bd42269c828704bfccbe9dd868769d094ce91f8cf86cac7da22bac29" "q-319519/field-1/867645cc65f2523d2da0f0bf9f79dcff4e4758e45f7d0d53126cc6ed4f8a9875"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319519" :question/id #uuid "784bc253-6dac-5f97-b706-d2c329fefc85" :question/math-academy-id "q-319519" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=-11-6\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/assets/ab2f3a9137c05ca19507e44d2bb2ef4b369c762189019265d8fe3bad34822fe7.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the third quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\pi <arg⁡(z)<\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan\\,(\\frac{6}{11})=0.499\\,346…\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=\\pi +0.499\\,346…≈3.64,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-319519/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a560db4d-e9d3-5d89-b2cd-c886f32db9df"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319519"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319581/field-1/7e35823d10f65dabc95929142749aca3c62d1af7b6ab33b0ab3042beceb457c5" :answer/id #uuid "bc94e163-e45a-5377-8083-3174d29e19d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319581/field-1/1571adfb82c9acb155ec7092053735f9ee1b7a1583de6614391981894a2d7495" :answer/id #uuid "ae3a11fe-83f7-51f8-a2b6-a312fc040f86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319581/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa1482a9-41f5-5769-ad7b-35fb1250adb2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319581/field-1/7e35823d10f65dabc95929142749aca3c62d1af7b6ab33b0ab3042beceb457c5" :answer-field/choices ["q-319581/field-1/7e35823d10f65dabc95929142749aca3c62d1af7b6ab33b0ab3042beceb457c5" "q-319581/field-1/1571adfb82c9acb155ec7092053735f9ee1b7a1583de6614391981894a2d7495"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319581" :question/id #uuid "46ec1ca3-4689-5158-9a8c-aaa28f0d5a07" :question/math-academy-id "q-319581" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find, **in radians**, the **exact value** of the argument of $z=8\\sqrt{3}-8\\text{i}.$\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/assets/78399e67e0ba69c1d7848a41aa5d4a5f8040fc578aab30a99f7e19ac86ece179.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<2\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the positive real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{8}{8\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{11\\pi }{6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-319581/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "54588722-bb80-54ca-b100-03aca39e0c17"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319581"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
